  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Monday)\nIssued at 119 PM MDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nVisible satellite shows clear skies for most of the Great Plains. An \nupper low spinning over northern CA/OR/NV is shedding upper clouds \nacross the northern Rockies. The inject of moisture into the \nnorthwest flow may bring these cirrus over the area tomorrow. 18Z \nsurface analysis depicts a warm front oriented zonally across South \nDakota slowly drifting northward and bringing hot and dry conditions \nto our area today. Highs over most of the area are in the upper 80s \nwith localized spots of 90+. Deep mixing will keep conditions dry. \nWestern South Dakota and northeastern Wyoming will see relative \nhumidities in the teens, while central SD will be closer the 30s. \nWinds today will be light for most of the area, however surface \ntroughing across south-central SD will support wind gusts between 30 \nand 35 mph. Although the overlap of wind and lack of moisture do not \nnecessitate a Red Flag Warning, fire weather concerns are still \nvalid today due to dry conditions. \n\nTemperatures for Tuesday will remain warm but not to the degree we \nwill see today. Highs in the mid 80s around the I90 latitude, \nlowering to 80 to the north and rising to the upper 80s to the \nsouth. Surface pressure falls will continue through the night as the \naforementioned trough progresses east. A cool front will move \nthrough the area on Tuesday as well, reaching the Rapid City area \nright around noon. Northwest winds behind the boundary will gust \naround 20 to 30 mph. \n\nTemperatures going forward will trend down through the \nend of the week. Things will stay warmer than average but high will \nbe in the 70s. Northwest upper flow dominates until the weekend. \nCurrent guidance swings a longwave trough down the west coast \nSaturday. As is stands now the GFS lags behind the current Euro \nmodels, but strengthen the overall system more. WPC forecasts show \nstrong cyclogenesis over the Dakotas Saturday morning, with front\ninduced precipitation chances starting Sunday and continuing \nthrough the start of next week. Column up to 700mb stays above \nfreezing so liquid precip is expected at this time. &&",
